/* book: lead: A dynamic gate stores its output on a capacitor instead of holding it with a pull-up network. A clock φ first precharges the dynamic node to VDD, then lets an nMOS network discharge it if the inputs say so. An N-input gate needs only N + 2 transistors, and its inputs drive only nMOS, so it is small and fast. The price is a clock on every gate, charge sharing, leakage and the rule that inputs may o */
