/* book Worked example 2: Q: The same dynamic node (50 fF) leaks 10 nA when the PDN is off and there is no keeper. The output stays valid while X loses at most 0.3 V. The node must hold for half a clock period. Find the lowest safe clock frequency.
   1. Hold time = C × ΔV / I = 50 fF × 0.3 V / 10 nA = 15 fC / 10 nA = 1.5 µs.
   2. Half the period must be no longer than 1.5 µs, so T ≤ 3 µs.
   3. f ≥ 1/3 µs = 333 kHz.
   Answer: The clock must not fall below about 333 kHz; for slower or stopped clocks a keeper is required. */
